{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-007",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 7,
  "title": "Proverbs 7",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 7",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 7,
  "sortOrder": 20007,
  "verseCount": 27,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thine heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Say unto wisdom, Thou art my sister; and call understanding thy kinswoman:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger which flattereth with her words.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "In the twilight, in the evening, in the black and dark night:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And, behold, there met him a woman with the attire of an harlot, and subtil of heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "(She is loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Now is she without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "So she caught him, and kissed him, and with an impudent face said unto him,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I have peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved works, with fine linen of Egypt.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For the goodman is not at home, he is gone a long journey:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "He hath taken a bag of money with him, and will come home at the day appointed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forced him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Till a dart strike through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it is for his life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Hearken unto me now therefore, O ye children, and attend to the words of my mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Let not thine heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "For she hath cast down many wounded: yea, many strong men have been slain by her.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:7:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Her house is the way to hell, going down to the chambers of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 7:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:7:27"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
